://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5570">SCP-5570</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5862">SCP-5862</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5900">SCP-5900</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5908">SCP-5908</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5909">SCP-5909</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5995">SCP-5995</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Placeholder</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/mcdoctorate-s-proposal">McDoctorate's Proposal</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>[REDACTED]</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1463">SCP-1463</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td><span style="font-family: 'Courier', monospace; font-weight: bold; margin: 2px 1px 1px 1px; background-color: #a3cef1; overflow-wrap: break-word;">Safe</span></td> <td>Object class is being lied about.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4428">Dr. Michaels</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>See Below</td> <td>Item constitutes several anomalies with distinct object classes.</td> <td><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-1399-ru">SCP-1399-RU</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4812">SCP-4812</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Unclassed</td> <td>Object classification has been intentionally avoided.</td> <td><a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/scp-200-fr">SCP-200-FR</a>, <a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/scp-226-fr">SCP-226-FR</a>, <a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/scp-1375-jp">SCP-1375-JP</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3939">SCP-3939</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Urgent reclassification required.</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3547">SCP-3547</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> </div> <h2><span>Informal Esoteric Classes</span></h2> <p>The following classes are presumed to have been influenced by an anomalous property or another third-party; generally, they are the result of an infectious memetic agent or an infohazard.</p> <div class="list"> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">►&nbsp;Informal&nbsp;Esoteric&nbsp;Classes&nbsp;◄</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▼&nbsp;Informal&nbsp;Esoteric&nbsp;Classes&nbsp;▼</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Class</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Appearances</th> </tr> <tr> <td><tt>Apologize.</tt></td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/shaggydredlocks-proposal">S. D. Locke's Proposal</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>At home, Bullshit, ??</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4205">SCP-4205</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Azathoth</td> <td>Item is incredibly dangerous and destructive.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4626">SCP-4626</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Beautiful</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2690">SCP-2690</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>BFF</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2790">SCP-2790</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td><span style="color: blue">CHALLENGE</span></td> <td>Item may or may not pose containment challenges.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5242">SCP-INTEGER</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Containment</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3408">Site-3408</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Dark Keter</td> <td>Item can neither be contained nor destroyed.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5166">SCP-5166</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Delicious</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5121">SCP-5121</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Dishwasher, Zenzizenzizenzic</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5145">SCP-5145</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Downy</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1425-765">SCP-1425-765</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Echelon</td> <td>Item is the highest priority of the Foundation.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5055">SCP-5055</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Former</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2602">SCP-2602, which used to be a library</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Friend</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5121">SCP-5121</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Glorious</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1561">SCP-1561</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>GOD</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5050">SCP-5050</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>In doubt</td> <td>Item's effect precludes the usage of extant object classes.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2685">SCP-2685</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Infohazardous Predator</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1463">SCP-1463</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Kronecker</td> <td>Item is no longer anomalous and is to be exempted from containment.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2062">SCP-2062</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Mendax</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4955">SCP-4955</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Nehemoth</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2998">SCP-2998</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Object Class</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3890">SCP-3890</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Oblique</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2786">SCP-2786</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Rapidus</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/too-slow">Too Slow</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td><tt>Robertson-Jackal</tt></td> <td>Item's name has been deliberately randomized in order to contain SCP-5856, a sociokinetic entity.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5856">SCP-5856</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Scarf</td> <td>Anomalous mutation if &quot;Safe&quot;.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-586">SCP-586</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>SCP-2357 poses no danger to anyone, although it very easily could have been made that way.</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2357">SCP-2357</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>&quot;Shadow's Crown&quot; Phenomenon</td> <td>Object class is analogous to Thaumiel.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4098">SCP-4098</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Spiteful motherfucker</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3020">SCP-3020</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Sunrays, Muted</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4391">Periapsis</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td><tt>UNDEFINED</tt></td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3942">UNDEFINED</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Whatever you want it to be, really. You're in charge here.</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3265">SCP-3265</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Youklid</td> <td>Incorrect spelling of &quot;Euclid&quot;.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4259">SCP-4259</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>53</td> <td>Item is highly intrusive, and has unknown capabilities and an unknown nature.</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scantron-s-proposal">Scantron's Proposal</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>▄█▐██</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/ura-1902">URA-1902</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> </div> <h2><span>Foreign Esoteric Classes</span></h2> <p>The following are object classes created by non-English affiliate branches of the Foundation which are considered &quot;Established&quot;.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-380369-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >4</a></sup></p> <p>Thank you to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ziakial" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2291501&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606876888" alt="Ziakial" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2291501)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ziakial" >Ziakial</a></span> for originally creating this list.</p> <div class="list"> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">►&nbsp;Foreign&nbsp;Esoteric&nbsp;Classes&nbsp;◄</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▼&nbsp;Foreign&nbsp;Esoteric&nbsp;Classes&nbsp;▼</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Class</th> <th>Definition</th> <th>Appearances</th> </tr> <tr> <td>Ain</td> <td>Item is capable of causing YK-Class events in the future that are unable to be dealt with.</td> <td><a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/scp-1690-jp">SCP-1690-JP</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Aisna</td> <td>Item generates anomalies, can be activated by a sentient being, and is related to a deity or reality's origin.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-int.wikidot.com/scp-001-it-abad">SCP-001-IT/ABAD</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Anesidora</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-cn-422">SCP-CN-422</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Asura</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/veleafer-s-proposal">Veleafer's Proposal (CN)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Atlas<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-380369-5" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >5</a></sup></td> <td>Item ensures the existence of mankind and/or the surrounding reality, and should not be restrained.</td> <td><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-1331-ru">SCP-1331-RU</a>, <a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-1399-ru">SCP-1399-RU</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Axiom</td> <td>Item is a universal truth.</td> <td><a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/r-00x-s-proposal">R-00X's Proposal (JP)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Bakkhos</td> <td>Item blurs the distinction between life and death, changing the significance and concept of containment and protection and collapsing normality.</td> <td><a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/jiraku-mogana-s-proposal">Jiraku Mogana's Proposal (JP)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Boltzmann</td> <td>Item is both necessary and inimical to the continuation of human life.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-int.wikidot.com/resazurin-s-proposal">Resazurin's Proposal</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Chhokmah</td> <td>Item is entangled with baseline and its containment would affect intelligent entities.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-cn-1900">SCP-CN-1900</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Compromised</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-cn-1025">SCP-CN-1025</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Daath</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/scp-411-jp">SCP-411-JP</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Ether</td> <td>Item's existence is not confirmed, and all information comes from witness testimony. Its containment procedures form a basis in case its existence is confirmed.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-pl.wikidot.com/scp-pl-206">SCP-PL-206</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Exist</td> <td>Item is existence itself.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-cn-366">SCP-CN-366</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Gleipnir</td> <td>Item continuously requires different/new forms of containment, thereby precluding standard classification.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-de.wikidot.com/scp-299-de">SCP-299-DE</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Interferelessed</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-cn-1390">SCP-CN-1390</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Jerusalem</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/fuban-s-proposal">Fuban's Proposal (CN)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Juggernaut</td> <td>Item is capable of causing the end of the world.</td> <td><a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/scp-654-jp">SCP-654-JP</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Malkuth</td> <td></td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/adamnpluto-s-proposal-i">AdamnPluto's Proposal (CN)</a>, <a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/okaka-onigiri-s-proposal">Okaka_Onigiri’s Proposal (JP)</a>, <a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/scp-090-jp">SCP-090-JP</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Necropsar</td> <td>Item currently has no reliable evidence supporting its existence in the standard Human History Process (H-001), but can be confirmed to potentially exist through observations made by the Department of Historical Observation and Planning regarding other Human History Processes and hidden signs currently in H-001.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-cn-1050">SCP-CN-1050</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Pantokratōr</td> <td>Item is too large for containment to be realistic.</td> <td><a href="http://ja.scp-wiki.net/indonootoko-s-proposal">Indonootoko's Proposal (JP)</a>, <a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/indonootoko-s-proposal-iii">Indonootoko's Proposal III (JP)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Tenebrarius</td> <td>The Foundation does not and cannot possess information about the item.</td> <td><a href="http://scp-wiki.net.pl/scp-pl-290">SCP-PL-290</a></td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="height: 25px"></div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nagiros" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4665703&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606876888" alt="Nagiros" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4665703)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nagiros" >Nagiros</a></span></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-380369-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Translated as &quot;Abnormal&quot; in some foreign branches.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-380369-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. A re-engineered designation of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/object-classes#toc9">the defunct object class</a> of the same name.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-380369-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. Original text: Ты - аномалия, опухоль миров</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-380369-4"><a href="javascript:;" >4</a>. Some translation errors may persist; informed archivists are welcome to update a foreign class' definition if they have the consent of the author or are otherwise certain of a better definition.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-380369-5"><a href="javascript:;" >5</a>. Original text: Атлант</div> </div> 
