				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5492</guid>
				<title>SCP-5492</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5492</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item#:&lt;/strong&gt; 5492&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Euclid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5492 is to be stored inside of a specific containment consisting of an immensely scant amount of room, and heaps of soundproof foam fastened against every wall as well as the roof and base of the room. Personnel may not enter SCP-5492&#039;s containment without specialized soundproof headphones in any condition, except D-class personnel for further research of this anomalous entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If by any circumstance SCP-5492 is to be heard and Subject is still alive, the personnel must be escorted out of the containment of SCP-5492 for further research due to the lack of knowledge on SCP-5492. Subject shall report for psychiatric analysis every 4 days and, depending on the results, Subject shall remain isolated until further examination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5492 is a speaker-like object produced somewhere in the 1800s, probably tracing back to 1877. Object#: 5492 is a half-rotten spruce cuboid, plated with metal speakers made with aluminium. Its main colour is white due to the clear lack of pigmentation in SCP-5492&#039;s shape, making the wood hard to classify to the eye.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;at the first glances, SCP-5492 seems almost innocuous to someone, but when out of containment SCP-5492 emits an ear-piercing high-frequency noise that leaves all personnel critically suicidal and most personnel are drawn to insanity and commit suicide, even going as far as to using their teeth to commit suicide. Reports on D-class surviving, though slim, have been shown that &amp;quot;the noise is so dreadful it&#039;s better to die than live to remember the horror&amp;quot; - Which was said by a test subject.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When multiple people enter the containment with the unfathomable entity, the results shown for the tests are not much different. In the 1950s multiple D-class personnel, around 4, were chosen to go into SCP-5492&#039;s containment for testing, 1 was still alive but badly injured due to self-inflicted harm and the other 3 were dead from fatal homocidal actions. When the surviving Subject made it out of the containment he was insane and instead of being suicidal he was critically homicidal instead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footer-wikiwalk-nav&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#171; &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5491&quot;&gt;SCP-5491&lt;/a&gt; | SCP-5492 | &lt;a class=&quot;newpage&quot; href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5493&quot;&gt;SCP-5493&lt;/a&gt; &amp;#187;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cocoaizblu&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6899557&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606876889&quot; alt=&quot;CocoaIzBlu&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6899557)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cocoaizblu&quot;  &gt;CocoaIzBlu&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
